[task-01] The rating a criterion gets for its test evidence is derived from the
    judgements the review has already recorded about the ways a change could fail that
    criterion and about whether each candidate test would fail on each of them. The
    tests the review prescribes are derived from those same judgements. So is the
    conclusion the review reaches. The older judgement of which tests bear on which
    criterion, and of whether a test discriminates, is removed.
    -> test-evidence-rating-derived-from-recorded-judgements  [invariant/explicit]
       The rating a criterion gets for its test evidence is derived from the judgements
       the review has already recorded about the ways a change could fail that criterion
       and about whether each candidate test would fail on each of them.
    -> test-prescriptions-derived-from-judgements  [functional/explicit]
       The tests the review prescribes are derived from the same judgements already
       recorded about how a change could fail the criterion and whether each candidate
       test would fail on each of them.
    -> conclusion-derived-from-recorded-judgements  [invariant/explicit]
       The review conclusion is derived from the judgements the review has already
       recorded about how a change could fail the criterion and about whether each
       candidate test would fail on each of those failures.
    -> remove-older-test-judgement  [invariant/explicit]
       The review no longer records the older judgement of which tests bear on which
       criterion, or whether a test discriminates.

[constraint-01] A recorded way of failing is covered when some candidate test would fail
    if the delivered code failed that way. A criterion all of whose recorded ways of
    failing are covered is strongly supported; one where some are covered is partially
    supported; one where none are, while candidate tests exist, is nominally supported.
    Where no candidate test exists, or the judgement could not be reached, the outcomes
    the review already has for those cases stand.
    -> coverage-from-failing-way  [functional/explicit]
       A recorded way of failing is covered when some candidate test would fail if the
       delivered code failed that way.
    -> rating-by-coverage-completeness  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion all of whose recorded ways of failing are covered is strongly
       supported; one where some are covered is partially supported; one where none are,
       while candidate tests exist, is nominally supported.
    -> preserve-existing-outcomes-when-unevaluable  [invariant/explicit]
       Where no candidate test exists, or the judgement could not be reached, the
       outcomes the review already has for those cases stand.

[constraint-02] Every rating the report shows names how many of that criterion's
    recorded ways of failing are covered, and how many were recorded.
    -> rating-shows-covered-and-total-failures  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Every report rating names how many of the criterion's recorded ways of failing
       are covered, and how many were recorded.

[constraint-03] A criterion for which the review recorded no plausible way of failing,
    and said why, gets an outcome of its own, neither strongly supported nor
    unsupported, and the report says test evidence cannot be obtained for it.
    -> no-plausible-failure-outcome  [functional/explicit]
       A criterion with no recorded plausible way of failing, and with an explanation
       for that, receives its own outcome that is neither strongly supported nor
       unsupported, and the report states that test evidence cannot be obtained for it.

[constraint-04] Every test the review recommends names one recorded way of failing that
    no candidate test would fail on, and that record carries a link to the criterion
    text it comes from.
    -> recommended-test-names-failing-way  [test_demand/explicit]
       Every recommended test names one recorded way of failing that no candidate test
       would fail on, and the recommendation includes a link to the criterion text it
       comes from.

[constraint-05] A recommendation asking for evidence the review already holds cannot be
    produced.
    -> no-redundant-recommendation  [functional/explicit]
       A recommendation that asks for evidence the review already holds is not produced.

[constraint-06] The ratings keep the names they have today, and what each of them means
    is unchanged.
    -> keep-rating-names  [compatibility/explicit]
       The ratings keep the names they have today, and what each of them means is
       unchanged.

[constraint-07] Where the review's measured accuracy is reported, that report says the
